Clean commit. Here's what I implemented:

ToolFailureTracker — A shared `Arc<Mutex<HashMap<String, u32>>>` that tracks consecutive failures per tool name. When a tool succeeds, its counter resets to 0. When it fails, the counter increments. Different tool names track independently.

RecoveryHintTool — A thin wrapper around any AgentTool that:
• On success: resets the failure counter, returns result unchanged
• On `ToolError::Failed: increments the counter, appends 💡 Recovery hint: <hint> from prompt_retry::tool_recovery_hint()` to the error message
• On other errors (NotFound, InvalidArgs, Cancelled): still counts as failure for escalation but passes through unchanged

`with_recovery_hints()` — Helper function matching the existing pattern (`with_truncation, with_auto_check`). Takes a shared tracker so all tools in a session share the same failure counts.

4 tests — All pass:
1. `test_recovery_hint_tool_success_resets_counter` — counter goes to 0 after success
2. test_recovery_hint_tool_appends_hint_on_failure — error includes original message + recovery hint
3. test_recovery_hint_tool_escalates_on_repeated_failure — attempt 1 gets diagnostic hint, attempt 2 gets escalated alternative-tool hint
4. `test_tool_failure_tracker_independent_per_tool` — bash and edit_file track separately; success on one doesn't affect the other

